WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.120
What's the last thing anyone expected&nbsp;
to see in the first episode of She-Hulk?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:10.960
How about busted tech from MCU Phase 2? Here's&nbsp;
the history behind the surprising memento.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:15.280
The Marvel Cinematic Universe has thrilled&nbsp;
audiences on the big and small screen for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:20.640
more than a decade, and in all that time there's&nbsp;
only been one in-universe version of the Hulk.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.040
Bruce Banner was originally played by Edward&nbsp;
Norton in "The Incredible Hulk" before Mark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:29.840
Ruffalo came aboard for "The Avengers" — but&nbsp;
it's the same character in the MCU. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:36.000
the hero has been joined by a brand new Jade&nbsp;
Giant, Jennifer Walters, also known as She-Hulk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.200
played by Tatiana Maslany of "Orphan Black" fame.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.800
Jen gets her powers from Bruce's blood when they&nbsp;
get into a car accident due to a Sakaarian ship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.200
showing up out of nowhere — a seeming&nbsp;
nod to the "World War Hulk" comics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:53.600
The series kicks things off by establishing&nbsp;
a fun dynamic between the two cousins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:58.720
as "Professor Hulk" tries to teach Jen&nbsp;
everything there is to know about being a Hulk.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:03.280
Speaking to Access Hollywood in February,&nbsp;
Ruffalo had high praise for Maslany

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:09.760
"Frickin' legendary as the She-Hulk.&nbsp;
I'm passing the 'banner' onto her."

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:10.720
Ruffalo added,

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.760
"There are some really good, funny, cool, long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:17.520
long scenes between Professor and&nbsp;
her. We've never really seen the Hulk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.520
interact with people the way he does in&nbsp;
that show. It'll be really interesting."

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.080
Bruce and Jen spend plenty of time in&nbsp;
the isolated Mexican laboratory where the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:30.800
scientist learned to merge his two selves in&nbsp;
the time between "Avengers: Infinity War,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:35.440
and "Avengers: Endgame." But when Walters is&nbsp;
wandering around the building, she finds a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:41.040
bittersweet Iron Man memento that has us all&nbsp;
in our feelings. Here's why it's so familiar.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.320
Although "She-Hulk" is obviously&nbsp;
about Jennifer Walters and how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:49.360
she balances her legal career alongside her&nbsp;
burgeoning responsibilities as a superhero,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.520
the show also takes the opportunity to&nbsp;
look at Bruce Banner a little more closely.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.560
Episode 1 reveals that Bruce spent a lot of&nbsp;
time with Tony Stark in the five-year "Blip" gap&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.880
after "Avengers: Infinity War," because&nbsp;
the billionaire playboy philanthropist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.840
funded his laboratory. They even built a&nbsp;
beach-side bar together to have some fun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:12.698
even in a traumatic time. But Bruce seems&nbsp;
to have done more of the work than his pal.

00:02:12.885 --> 00:02:17.600
"Well, Tony mostly drank, just sat&nbsp;
around, like, complaining about Steve."

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:22.720
When Jen is wandering through the house, she finds&nbsp;
a ruined Iron Man helmet that Bruce is clearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:27.920
keeping to remember his fallen friend. It seems&nbsp;
like the black-and-gold helmet could be from a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:33.360
Mark XX Python suit, which briefly shows up with&nbsp;
several other suits at the end of "Iron Man 3."

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.320
Fans will remember that Bruce briefly appears&nbsp;
in the post-credits scene of the 2013 movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:42.640
nodding off while listening to Tony&nbsp;
ramble on. But the Mark XX suit blows up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:47.280
on Tony's orders, after the final big&nbsp;
battle in "Iron Man 3," so it's way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:52.800
more likely that the memento is actually an&nbsp;
Iron Legion droid head from the "Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:58.000
Age of Ultron" era. These unwearable suits&nbsp;
were ultimately used against the Avengers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:02.480
when Ultron — who was developed with&nbsp;
Bruce's help — took control of them.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:07.120
This little memento reminds us that Tony&nbsp;
and Bruce had a real friendship that thrived&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:12.000
outside of saving the world. When the two first&nbsp;
meet in "The Avengers," Tony tells Bruce that he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:17.760
a big fan of his, especially when he grows into an&nbsp;
"enormous green rage monster." Over the years we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:22.960
see them connect and grow as friends, working on&nbsp;
projects and driving around in supercars together.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:28.640
Using a small part of "She-Hulk: Attorney at Law"&nbsp;
to look a little closer at Hulk's character arc is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:34.400
a clever move from Marvel. After all, the giant&nbsp;
hero hasn't had his own solo movie since 2008,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.440
since the distribution rights for&nbsp;
the character are at Universal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:42.543
so any MCU Hulk action is a welcome turn&nbsp;
of events, even on the small screen.

